WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.078 --> 00:00:07.786
That afternoon Tom was eating nuts in his room.

2
00:00:07.787 --> 00:00:14.822
When someone knocked on the door, he quickly hid the nuts and nutcracker in the armored glove.

3
00:00:14.823 --> 00:00:19.503
"Come in!" Tom called, trying to act normally.

4
00:00:19.504 --> 00:00:23.134
Tom was surprised when a thin boy entered the room.

5
00:00:23.135 --> 00:00:26.684
He appeared to be about 12 years old.

6
00:00:26.685 --> 00:00:31.149
With his head bowed, he dropped to his knees before Tom.

7
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:37.790
"Rise, lad," Tom said. "Who are you, and what do you want?"

8
00:00:37.791 --> 00:00:41.319
The boy stood and looked at Tom with some concern.

9
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:46.494
He'd heard the rumors about the prince's illness and knew he shouldn't act surprised.

10
00:00:46.495 --> 00:00:49.144
But he couldn't help himself.

11
00:00:49.145 --> 00:00:52.714
"Oh, surely you must remember me, Your Majesty.

12
00:00:52.715 --> 00:00:57.178
I'm Marlow, your whipping boy."

13
00:00:57.179 --> 00:01:02.667
Tom had no idea what a whipping boy did, so he couldn't pretend to know Marlow.

14
00:01:02.668 --> 00:01:07.856
"Lord Hertford should have told me about him," Tom thought.

15
00:01:07.857 --> 00:01:12.098
But Tom knew that Lord Hertford couldn't be by his side every minute.

16
00:01:12.099 --> 00:01:16.768
Something similar was bound to happen again.

17
00:01:16.769 --> 00:01:22.934
Tom needed a way to cope by himself, and he decided to practice on this boy.

18
00:01:22.935 --> 00:01:29.109
"My whipping boy . . ." Tom tapped his chin as if he was thinking.

19
00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:37.205
"Hmm. I dimly remember you, but my illness has affected my mind.

20
00:01:37.206 --> 00:01:40.494
Can you give me a little clue about yourself?

21
00:01:40.495 --> 00:01:44.266
That sometimes jogs my memory."

22
00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:50.574
"Do you remember a few days ago when you made three mistakes during your Greek lesson?"

23
00:01:50.575 --> 00:02:00.137
"Maybe . . ." Meanwhile Tom thought he'd probably make forty mistakes if he really was taking Greek.

24
00:02:00.138 --> 00:02:05.384
"Your teacher was going to whip me because you were too lazy to study."

25
00:02:05.385 --> 00:02:12.502
Tom was astonished. "Whip you for something that was my fault?"

26
00:02:12.503 --> 00:02:17.037
"Yes, your teachers always whip me when you fail at your lessons.

27
00:02:17.038 --> 00:02:23.336
No one may strike you, so I take your punishments for you," Marlow explained patiently.

28
00:02:23.337 --> 00:02:27.320
"That's my job, and I get paid for it."

29
00:02:27.321 --> 00:02:31.402
Tom thought this was a very strange way to earn a living.

30
00:02:31.403 --> 00:02:36.392
"And has my Greek teacher beaten you this week as planned?"

31
00:02:36.393 --> 00:02:37.583
"No, Your Majesty.

32
00:02:37.584 --> 00:02:43.559
The whipping was scheduled for today but was canceled because we're in mourning for King Henry.

33
00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:48.212
So . . ." Marlow hesitated.

34
00:02:48.213 --> 00:02:52.777
"So I've taken a chance and come to remind you of your promise.

35
00:02:52.778 --> 00:02:57.181
You offered to plead with your teacher on my behalf."

36
00:02:57.182 --> 00:03:04.468
"Ah, now I remember. Yes, I'll talk to him for you."

37
00:03:04.469 --> 00:03:07.358
"Thank you, sir." Marlow paused.

38
00:03:07.359 --> 00:03:13.257
"Some people would say you've been kind enough, but I have another favor to ask."

39
00:03:13.258 --> 00:03:17.125
"Go on. I'm feeling in a generous mood."

40
00:03:17.126 --> 00:03:21.496
Tom encouraged Marlow to sit down.

41
00:03:21.497 --> 00:03:25.854
"Now that you're king, you can do whatever you want.

42
00:03:25.855 --> 00:03:29.412
Which means you can stop having lessons.

43
00:03:29.413 --> 00:03:34.112
But if you do that, there will be no need for a whipping boy.

44
00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:39.603
I don't like being whipped, but I'll lose my job and my home here."

45
00:03:39.604 --> 00:03:42.508
Marlow dropped to his knees again.

46
00:03:42.509 --> 00:03:46.539
"Please, sir, don't turn me out on the street!"

47
00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.218
Tom liked Marlow and was happy to help.

48
00:03:50.219 --> 00:03:54.769
"Rise, Marlow.

49
00:03:54.770 --> 00:04:02.280
From here on, all whippings will be banned in the palace, but you'll have a job for life."

50
00:04:02.281 --> 00:04:06.974
Marlow heaved a sigh of relief.

51
00:04:06.975 --> 00:04:13.196
"Oh, thank you, sir! But what will I do?"

52
00:04:13.197 --> 00:04:16.822
"You can answer my questions," Tom said.

53
00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:22.323
"You know a lot about what goes on here, and it helps my memory to talk to you.

54
00:04:22.324 --> 00:04:27.171
Let's start with . . ."

55
00:04:27.172 --> 00:04:32.841
After an hour Tom had gained valuable information about royal people and events.

56
00:04:32.842 --> 00:04:35.381
And Marlow was pleased too.

57
00:04:35.382 --> 00:04:39.369
He felt that he had helped the king to get better.

58
00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:42.944
"You've earned your wages today," Tom said.

59
00:04:42.945 --> 00:04:50.287
"I want you to visit me every day and update me on what's happening."

60
00:04:50.288 --> 00:04:56.658
Soon after Marlow left Tom's room, Lord Hertford arrived.

61
00:04:56.659 --> 00:05:02.278
"I'm sorry to bring disturbing news, Your Majesty."

62
00:05:02.279 --> 00:05:04.651
Lord Hertford took a deep breath.

63
00:05:04.652 --> 00:05:10.492
"Your advisers fear that news of your illness has leaked.

64
00:05:10.493 --> 00:05:14.682
They want you to start dining regularly in public.

65
00:05:14.683 --> 00:05:19.618
Seeing you in good health will reassure people."

66
00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:23.246
An hour ago this news would have surprised Tom.

67
00:05:23.247 --> 00:05:28.703
But Marlow had heard gossip about the advisers' plan and passed it on to Tom.

68
00:05:28.704 --> 00:05:35.105
"I can understand why they'd think this was a good idea," Tom said.

69
00:05:35.106 --> 00:05:40.005
Lord Hertford was relieved that the king was acting more like himself.

70
00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:43.856
He decided to test Tom with a few questions.

71
00:05:43.857 --> 00:05:48.758
Thanks to Marlow, Tom was able to respond intelligently.

72
00:05:48.759 --> 00:05:54.795
Encouraged by Tom's replies, Lord Hertford asked one last question.

73
00:05:54.796 --> 00:05:59.790
"Do you remember where you put the Great Seal?"

74
00:05:59.791 --> 00:06:08.606
"No." Tom shook his head. "What does that look like?"

75
00:06:08.607 --> 00:06:11.612
Lord Hertford hid his disappointment.

76
00:06:11.613 --> 00:06:15.092
The king was obviously still not well.

77
00:06:15.093 --> 00:06:18.128
"It doesn't really matter, Your Highness.

78
00:06:18.129 --> 00:06:32.915
Now that King Henry is dead, you'll soon have a new seal of your own."

